<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U says gets EU approval for Xalatan.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U says gets EU approval for Xalatan.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs group Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said on Thursday its eye agent Xalatan received European Union (EU) approval after a mutual recognition procedure at the British Medicines Control Agency.  </p>
<p>&quot;As the procedure for mutual agreement for Xalatan is ready, the drug will be registered and launched in European Union member countries,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The approval of national registrations in those countries is expected in the autumn.&quot;</p>
<p>Xalatan has also been filed for registration in Japan, Canada and Australia as well as other countries, the group said.</p>
<p>Xalatan treats glaucoma from which about six million Europeans suffer, P&amp;U said. About two million patients are currently being treated.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
